# Central Error Handling

## Core Requirements
- Wrap all entry points with error handler
- Standardize error responses
- Log errors externally (Sentry/Logger)

## Standard Error Response
```typescript
interface StandardError {
  success: boolean;
  code: string;
  message: string;
}
```

## Implementation Guidelines
1. Use error boundaries for React components
2. Implement consistent error handling in API calls
3. Centralize error logging
4. Provide user-friendly error messages

## Error Handling Locations
- API Integration: [src/integrations/supabase/client.ts](mdc:src/integrations/supabase/client.ts)
- Auth Context: [src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx](mdc:src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx)
- Config Management: [src/lib/config.ts](mdc:src/lib/config.ts)

## Best Practices
- Never swallow errors silently
- Always log unexpected errors
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Handle both API and runtime errors consistently

